// Direct3D 12 COM test harness — Foundation `Test`-construct shape (kik).
//
// Each Test drives the real Direct3D 12 loader on the host: it creates a device
// through `D3D12CreateDevice` and then calls a method on that device through
// the device's own vtable, which is the path every D3D12 call in this package
// will take. Nothing here asserts a marker — the values checked are an
// `HRESULT` from the driver and a reference count from `Release`.
//
// Windows only, in the same way the Metal suite is Apple only: there is no
// `d3d12.dll` to open elsewhere, and a test that passed without one would be
// asserting nothing. Run with:
//
//   KIRA_PURE_TEST=1 kira test --backend vm tests/d3d12_kik
//   KIRA_PURE_TEST=1 kira test --backend llvm tests/d3d12_kik
//
// Both backends must agree, because the whole point of the call builder is that
// a COM call is made the same way whether Kira is interpreting or compiled.
